00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.090
Nicole: We can see that threats to
organisations can come from a range of

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:09.849
sources external and internal, ‘threat
actors’ may even attack home workers

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:15.489
or users via a phishing email, text,
phone call, or by using cleverly worded

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:19.660
messages on other communication systems
such as Slack or Microsoft Teams.

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:24.450
This can then make them become the
'threat actor' unintentionally,

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:28.630
therefore everyone should be aware of
the importance of safeguarding their

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:31.030
data and protecting their devices.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.149
So, what are some of the
motives for external threats

00:00:35.619 --> 00:00:40.150
One of the most common motives for
external threats is for financial gain

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:45.310
by getting access to customers financial
details such as credit or debit card data.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:50.380
They also can access email addresses
and login credentials gaining access

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:55.660
to a great many personal computers
and subsequently more financial gain.

00:00:56.310 --> 00:01:00.120
Bank details can be used to
access bank accounts and misdirect

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:04.099
individuals into believing they are
being contacted by their own banks.

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:10.570
By using ransomware external threat
actors can also hold a company to ransom

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:13.030
and affect its security credibility.

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:17.330
They can also impact a company's
profitability as they may

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:18.500
not be able to function.

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:22.200
This can make it easier for other
businesses to take their place.

00:01:23.099 --> 00:01:26.050
Now let’s look at motives
for insider threats.

00:01:26.889 --> 00:01:30.539
Financial gain can also be a
motive for insider threats where

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:35.890
unscrupulous employees may access
customers financial details, data and

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:38.300
databases and sell them on to others.

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:44.070
They may also want to act maliciously
passing on secrets or information to

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:49.300
other companies or organisations for
financial gain or to undermine a company.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:54.690
It’s also becoming increasingly common
for cybercriminals to try to “recruit”

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:59.410
people working inside companies, who
have privileged access to systems.

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:03.959
They get them to share their access and
in return they get a cut of the profits.

